Fixes #452

## Description

This PR always **enforces** no newline between overload signatures.

### Why not allow users to choose to add a newline if they want (`newlinesInside: ignore` behavior)

For two reasons:
- I don't think there is a use case where someone would want to have a newline between overload signatures.
- This fixes a pain that can happen when sorting elements together: see the example below.

#### Example without enforcing no newline

Configuration

```js
{
  newlinesBetween: "ignore"
}
```

Initial code
```ts
class Class {
  public b(parameter: number): string;
  public b(parameter: string): number;
  public b(parameter: number | string): number | string {
    return parameter;
  }

  a: string;
}
```

Code after linting

```ts
class Class {
  a: string;
  public b(parameter: number): string;
  public b(parameter: string): number;

  public b(parameter: number | string): number | string {
    return parameter;
  }
}
```

